  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "module": "std.ocr",
  "generated": "scripts/gen_tki.py (137.12) derives every arity here from the glue. Parameter and return TYPES are not derivable -- every pointer, every integer and every f64 is i64 in the toke ABI -- so the types below were written over the generated skeleton, which is exactly the contract that script documents: it is additive and arity-correcting, and an export that already exists keeps its hand-written types verbatim. Re-running it leaves this file unchanged. Story 135.6.",
  "exports": [
    {
      "kind": "type",
      "name": "ocrrun",
      "comment": "std.pdf's $textrun, slot for slot. Six of the seven fields are identical in name, type and position; the seventh differs in name only, same type and same slot, so the two records are bit-identical under the flat-i64-block struct ABI. A PDF knows the font size and not the confidence; a recogniser knows the confidence and not the font size. x/y/width/height are PIXELS OF THE SOURCE IMAGE with the origin at the BOTTOM-LEFT and y increasing upward -- std.pdf's convention, not the raster one, so a consumer sorts $ocrrun and $textrun with the identical comparison.",
      "fields": [
        {"name": "text",       "type": "str"},
        {"name": "page",       "type": "i64"},
        {"name": "x",          "type": "f64"},
        {"name": "y",          "type": "f64"},
        {"name": "width",      "type": "f64"},
        {"name": "height",     "type": "f64"},
        {"name": "confidence", "type": "f64"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "type",
      "name": "ocrerr",
      "is_sum": true,
      "comment": "$noengine is the one requirement 5 of story 135.6 turns on: on a platform with no recogniser this module fails, and never returns empty text. Empty text reads as 'no content', which is a different and wrong answer -- the same defect std.pdf refuses with a distinct $encrypted.",
      "fields": [
        {"name": "$noengine",   "type": "str"},
